module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Stalk
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.Quasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.StalkFreeCover
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SheafHomLeftExact
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Stalks of the sheaf of homomorphisms

Let `Rc` be a sheaf of commutative rings on a topological space `X`, let `O_X = structureSheaf Rc`
be the underlying sheaf of rings, and let `F` and `G` be `O_X`-modules. For a point `x : X` there
is a canonical map
`SheafHom_{O_X}(F, G)_x → Hom_{O_{X,x}}(F_x, G_x)`,
sending the germ at `x` of a local homomorphism `φ : F|_U → G|_U` to the induced map on stalks.

This file constructs that canonical map, as an `O_{X,x}`-linear map, and characterizes it by its
effect on germs.

## Main definitions

* `stalkMap φ hxU`: for `φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U` a homomorphism of `O_U`-modules and `x ∈ U`,
  the induced map `F_x ⟶ G_x` of stalks; `stalkLinearMap φ hxU` is the same map bundled as an
  `O_{X,x}`-linear map.
* `sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x`: the canonical `O_{X,x}`-linear map
  `SheafHom_{O_X}(F, G)_x →ₗ[O_{X,x}] (F_x →ₗ[O_{X,x}] G_x)`, built from a presentation
  `H : SheafHom Rc F G` of the internal hom
    (`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SheafHomLeftExact`).
* `SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv Rc F G H x`: a linear equivalence from the stalk of the internal hom
  to the module of homomorphisms of the stalks, together with the requirement that its action on
  germs is the canonical one.
* `appAt hWU φ`, `resLE M h`, `germAt M W x hx`: notation-level abbreviations for the
  component of a homomorphism of `O_U`-modules at an open `W ≤ U`, for a restriction map, and
  for a germ, spelled so that the `Rc.obj`-module structures are the ones Lean finds by
  instance search.
* `sheafHomStalkLinearEquivOfFinitePresentation H x`: Stacks 01CP itself — the canonical map as
  a linear equivalence, for `F` of finite presentation.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalGenerators`: section-level finite-type data on a neighbourhood of
  `x` — finitely many sections which generate locally — obtained from
  `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_localGenerators`.

## Main results

* `stalkMap_germ`: the defining formula `(stalkMap φ hxU) (germ_x t) = germ_x (φ t)` for a
  section `t` over an open `W ≤ U`.
* `sheafHomStalkLinearMap_germ`: the canonical map sends the germ of a local homomorphism and the
  germ of a local section to the germ of the evaluation. This is the equation that appears as the
  `germ_apply` field of `SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv`.
* `sheafHomStalkLinearMap_unique`: an `O_{X,x}`-linear map out of the stalk of the internal hom
  satisfying that germ formula equals `sheafHomStalkLinearMap`. So the germ formula pins the
  canonical map down, and `SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv` really is the assertion that *the canonical
  map* is an isomorphism rather than the weaker assertion that source and target happen to be
  isomorphic.
* `SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv.bijective` and `SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv.ofBijective`: the two
  directions identifying `SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv Rc F G H x` with bijectivity of the canonical
  map. Together they reduce Stacks 01CP to the single statement
  `Function.Bijective (sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x)`.

* `injective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localGenerators`,
  `surjective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localPresentation` and
  `bijective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localPresentation`: **the germ-local form of Stacks 01CP.**
  The two halves hold as soon as `F` has local generators, resp. a local presentation, *at the
  single point `x`* — data on one neighbourhood of `x`, with no hypothesis on `F` elsewhere. That
  is all the arguments ever use; the finiteness instances below enter only to produce that data.
  This is the form in which 01CP applies to a complex which is strictly perfect only near `x`.
* `injective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap` and `surjective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap`: the two halves of
  Stacks 01CP, and `sheafHomStalkLinearEquivOfFinitePresentation` assembles them into the
  tagged statement. Injectivity uses only that `F` is locally generated by finitely many
  sections, and is therefore stated for `F` of finite *type*; surjectivity uses the relations as
  well and needs finite presentation.

## Implementation notes on the finiteness hypotheses

The finiteness hypothesis is consumed through section-level data on a neighbourhood of `x`, in
two strengths. `Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalGenerators` carries finitely many sections over a
neighbourhood of `x` together with the statement that they generate locally at every point of
it, and `nonempty_localGenerators` (below) extracts it from Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` by choosing a member of the covering in
`SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData` that contains `x`. `LocalPresentation`
(`StalkFreeCover`) additionally carries finitely many relations and the statement that they
generate all relations locally, and `nonempty_localPresentation` extracts it from
`SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation`; `LocalPresentation.toLocalGenerators` forgets the
relations. With that data in hand both halves of 01CP are elementary germ chases, and no
exactness statement about the stalk functor is needed.

Surjectivity does need one categorical input, isolated in `exists_factor_of_epi`: in the abelian
category of sheaves of modules an epimorphism is the cokernel of its kernel, so a map out of a
finite free module which annihilates the kernel of the presentation factors through `F|_V`.

## Implementation notes

The stalk of a sheaf of modules is the filtered colimit of its groups of sections over the open
neighbourhoods of `x`, taken in `Ab`; the `O_{X,x}`-module structure on it is Mathlib's instance
from `Mathlib/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Stalk.lean`, whose characterizing property is
`PresheafOfModules.germ_smul`. That instance is stated for a presheaf of modules over a presheaf
of rings of the form `R ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat`, so it is *not* found by instance search
for a term whose type is spelled `PresheafOfModules (structureSheaf Rc).obj` (unifying the two
would need higher-order unification). The abbreviation `commVal` retypes `M.val` in the form
Lean can use, and `appAt`/`resLE`/`germAt` are phrased through it; this is why those abbreviations
exist, and every statement below is spelled with them.

A homomorphism `φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U` only provides maps `F(W) → G(W)` for opens `W ≤ U`,
while the stalk at `x` is a colimit over *all* open neighbourhoods of `x`. Rather than invoking
cofinality of `{W | W ≤ U}` in `OpenNhds x`, the cocone `stalkCocone` is defined on all of
`OpenNhds x` by first restricting a section over `W` to `W ⊓ U`. This is elementary and makes the
germ formula `stalkMap_germ_inf` hold by construction; `stalkMap_germ` specializes it to `W ≤ U`,
where `W ⊓ U = W`.

Everything lives in the single universe `v` of `X : TopCat.{v}`. This is forced, not chosen:
Mathlib's module structure on the stalk of a presheaf of modules is only available for a presheaf
of modules valued in `ModuleCat.{v}` over a presheaf of rings valued in `RingCat.{v}` on a space
in `TopCat.{v}`, which is also the universe in which `SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)` and
`SheafHom Rc F G` are taken.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CP)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace

universe v u'

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

open _root_.SheafOfModules

variable {X : TopCat.{v}} {R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type v)) RingCat.{v}}

/-- Section-level finite-type data for a sheaf of modules on a neighbourhood of a point:
finitely many sections over a neighbourhood of `x` which generate `M` locally at every point of
that neighbourhood. This is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalPresentation` with the relations
forgotten, and it is all that the injectivity half of Stacks 01CP consumes. -/
structure LocalGenerators (M : SheafOfModules.{v} R) (x : X) where
  /-- the neighbourhood on which the generating sections live -/
  nhd : Opens X
  mem_nhd : x ∈ nhd
  /-- index type of the generators -/
  Gen : Type v
  fintypeGen : Fintype Gen
  /-- the generating sections -/
  gens : Gen → ToType (M.val.obj (op nhd))
  /-- the generators generate locally -/
  generates : ∀ ⦃V : Opens X⦄ (f : V ⟶ nhd) (t : ToType (M.val.obj (op V))) (y : X), y ∈ V →
    ∃ (W : Opens X) (g : W ⟶ V), y ∈ W ∧ ∃ c : Gen → ToType (R.obj.obj (op W)),
      res M g t = ∑ k : Gen, c k • res M (g ≫ f) (gens k)

attribute [instance] LocalGenerators.fintypeGen

/-- The generating sections of a local presentation, with the relations forgotten. -/
def LocalPresentation.toLocalGenerators {M : SheafOfModules.{v} R} {x : X}
    (LP : LocalPresentation M x) : LocalGenerators M x where
  nhd := LP.nhd
  mem_nhd := LP.mem_nhd
  Gen := LP.Gen
  fintypeGen := LP.fintypeGen
  gens := LP.gens
  generates := LP.generates

section GeneratingSections

variable (M : SheafOfModules.{v} R) {U : Opens X} (σ : (M.over U).GeneratingSections)

/-- A family of generating sections of `M.over U`, read as sections of `M` over `U`. This is the
`Presentation`-free analogue of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.presGens`. -/
noncomputable def genGens (k : σ.I) : ToType (M.val.obj (op U)) :=
  (σ.s k).eval (op (Over.mk (𝟙 U)))

lemma genGens_π : σ.π = freeToOver M (genGens M σ) :=
  freeHomEquiv_symm_eq_freeToOver M _

lemma epi_freeToOver_genGens : Epi (freeToOver M (genGens M σ)) := by
  rw [← genGens_π]; exact σ.epi

end GeneratingSections

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01BN** in the finite-type case: a sheaf of modules of finite type
admits section-level generating data on a neighbourhood of every point. This is the finite-type
counterpart of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_localPresentation`, and it is what lets the
injectivity half of Stacks 01CP be stated for `F` of finite type. -/
theorem nonempty_localGenerators (M : SheafOfModules.{v} R) [M.IsFiniteType] (x : X) :
    Nonempty (LocalGenerators M x) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData M
  obtain ⟨i₀, hi₀⟩ : ∃ i, x ∈ q.X i := by
    have h : IsOpenCover q.X := (Opens.coversTop_iff (X : Type v) q.X).1 q.coversTop
    have hx : x ∈ (⨆ i, q.X i) := by rw [h.iSup_eq_top]; exact Opens.mem_top x
    simpa using hx
  have := hq.isFiniteType i₀
  have : Fintype (q.generators i₀).I := Fintype.ofFinite _
  have := epi_freeToOver_genGens M (q.generators i₀)
  exact ⟨{ nhd := q.X i₀
           mem_nhd := hi₀
           Gen := (q.generators i₀).I
           fintypeGen := inferInstance
           gens := genGens M (q.generators i₀)
           generates := generates_of_epi M (genGens M (q.generators i₀)) }⟩

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules.SheafHomStalk

variable {X : TopCat.{v}} {Rc : TopCat.Sheaf CommRingCat.{v} X}

/-- The underlying presheaf of modules of a sheaf of modules over the structure sheaf
`structureSheaf Rc`, retyped as a presheaf of modules over the *commutative* presheaf of rings
`Rc.obj`. This is the form in which Mathlib's module structures on sections and on stalks are
found by instance search. -/
noncomputable abbrev commVal (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) :
    PresheafOfModules.{v} (Rc.obj ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) := M.val

/-- The stalk `O_{X,x}` at `x` of a sheaf of commutative rings. -/
noncomputable abbrev ringStalk (Rc : TopCat.Sheaf CommRingCat.{v} X) (x : X) : CommRingCat.{v} :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := CommRingCat.{v}) Rc.obj x

/-- The stalk `M_x` at `x` of a sheaf of modules, an abelian group carrying a canonical
`O_{X,x}`-module structure. -/
noncomputable abbrev modStalk (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) (x : X) : Ab.{v} :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{v}) (commVal M).presheaf x

/-- The restriction map of a sheaf of modules along an inclusion of opens. -/
noncomputable abbrev resLE (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W W' : Opens X}
    (h : W' ≤ W) (t : (commVal M).obj (op W)) : (commVal M).obj (op W') :=
  (commVal M).map (homOfLE h).op t

/-- The germ at `x` of a section of a sheaf of modules. -/
noncomputable abbrev germAt (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) (W : Opens X) (x : X)
    (hx : x ∈ W) (t : (commVal M).obj (op W)) : modStalk M x :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.germ (C := Ab.{v}) (commVal M).presheaf W x hx t

variable {F G : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)}

section Basic

/-- Membership in an intersection of opens, as a declaration rather than an anonymous
constructor. Using this keeps the membership proofs opaque, which matters because a term
`(⟨hxW, hxU⟩ : x ∈ W ⊓ U)` is not type-correct at `rw`'s matching transparency and silently
blocks rewriting inside `germAt`. -/
lemma mem_inf {x : X} {W U : Opens X} (hxW : x ∈ W) (hxU : x ∈ U) : x ∈ W ⊓ U := ⟨hxW, hxU⟩

lemma resLE_resLE (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W W' W'' : Opens X}
    (h : W' ≤ W) (h' : W'' ≤ W') (t : (commVal M).obj (op W)) :
    resLE M h' (resLE M h t) = resLE M (h'.trans h) t :=
  (PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply (commVal M) (homOfLE h).op (homOfLE h').op t).symm.trans
    (PresheafOfModules.congr_map_apply (commVal M) (Subsingleton.elim _ _) t)

lemma germAt_add (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W : Opens X} {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ W) (t t' : (commVal M).obj (op W)) :
    germAt M W x hx (t + t') = germAt M W x hx t + germAt M W x hx t' :=
  map_add _ _ _

lemma germAt_zero (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W : Opens X} {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ W) : germAt M W x hx 0 = 0 :=
  map_zero _

@[simp]
lemma germAt_resLE (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W W' : Opens X} {x : X}
    (h : W' ≤ W) (hx : x ∈ W') (t : (commVal M).obj (op W)) :
    germAt M W' x hx (resLE M h t) = germAt M W x (h hx) t :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply (commVal M).presheaf (homOfLE h) x hx t

lemma germAt_smul (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W : Opens X} {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ W) (r : Rc.obj.obj (op W)) (t : (commVal M).obj (op W)) :
    germAt M W x hx (r • t) = TopCat.Presheaf.germ Rc.obj W x hx r • germAt M W x hx t :=
  PresheafOfModules.germ_smul (commVal M) x W hx r t

lemma resLE_smul (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W W' : Opens X} (h : W' ≤ W)
    (r : Rc.obj.obj (op W)) (t : (commVal M).obj (op W)) :
    resLE M h (r • t) = Rc.obj.map (homOfLE h).op r • resLE M h t :=
  PresheafOfModules.map_smul (commVal M) (homOfLE h).op r t

/-- Every element of a stalk is the germ of a section over some open neighbourhood. -/
lemma exists_germ_eq (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {x : X} (m : modStalk M x) :
    ∃ (W : Opens X) (hx : x ∈ W) (t : (commVal M).obj (op W)), germAt M W x hx t = m :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq (commVal M).presheaf m

end Basic

section Components

/-- The component at an open `W ≤ U` of a homomorphism `φ : F|_U ⟶ G|_U` of `O_U`-modules, as a
map from the sections of `F` over `W` to the sections of `G` over `W`. The site of `F.over U` is
the over-category `Over U`, so this is literally the component of `φ.val` at the object
`Over.mk (homOfLE hWU)`; the point of the abbreviation is that its source and target are spelled
through `commVal`, which is what makes the `Rc.obj`-module structures available. -/
noncomputable def appAt {U W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U)
    (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op W)) : (commVal (Rc := Rc) G).obj (op W) :=
  φ.val.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hWU))) t

lemma appAt_add {U W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U)
    (t t' : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op W)) :
    appAt hWU φ (t + t') = appAt hWU φ t + appAt hWU φ t' :=
  map_add _ _ _

lemma appAt_zero {U W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) :
    appAt hWU φ 0 = 0 :=
  map_zero _

lemma appAt_smul {U W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U)
    (r : Rc.obj.obj (op W)) (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op W)) :
    appAt hWU φ (r • t) = r • appAt hWU φ t :=
  (φ.val.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hWU)))).hom.map_smul r t

/-- The components of a sum of homomorphisms are the sums of the components. -/
lemma appAt_add_hom {U W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (φ ψ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U)
    (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op W)) :
    appAt hWU (φ + ψ) t = appAt hWU φ t + appAt hWU ψ t := rfl

/-- Naturality of the components: the component at `W' ≤ U` applied to a restricted section is
the restriction of the component at `W ≤ U`. -/
lemma appAt_res {U W W' : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (hW'W : W' ≤ W)
    (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op W)) :
    appAt (hW'W.trans hWU) φ (resLE F hW'W t) = resLE G hW'W (appAt hWU φ t) :=
  PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply φ.val
    (Y := op (Over.mk (homOfLE (hW'W.trans hWU)) : Over U))
    (X := op (Over.mk (homOfLE hWU) : Over U))
    (op (Over.homMk (homOfLE hW'W))) t

/-- Shrinking the open set on which a section is taken does not change the germ of the value of
a component of `φ`. -/
lemma germ_appAt {x : X} {U W W' : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (hW'W : W' ≤ W)
    (hxW' : x ∈ W') (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op W)) :
    germAt G W' x hxW' (appAt (hW'W.trans hWU) φ (resLE F hW'W t))
      = germAt G W x (hW'W hxW') (appAt hWU φ t) := by
  rw [appAt_res hWU hW'W φ t, germAt_resLE]

/-- The cocone compatibility underlying `stalkCocone`: restricting a section from `W` to
`W' ≤ W` before applying the component of `φ` over the intersection with `U` does not change the
resulting germ. -/
lemma germ_appAt_res_inf {x : X} {U W W' : Opens X} (hle : W' ≤ W) (hxW' : x ∈ W')
    (hxU : x ∈ U) (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op W)) :
    germAt G (W' ⊓ U) x (mem_inf hxW' hxU)
        (appAt (inf_le_right : W' ⊓ U ≤ U) φ (resLE F (inf_le_left : W' ⊓ U ≤ W') (resLE F hle t)))
      = germAt G (W ⊓ U) x (mem_inf (hle hxW') hxU)
          (appAt (inf_le_right : W ⊓ U ≤ U) φ (resLE F (inf_le_left : W ⊓ U ≤ W) t)) := by
  have h1 : W' ⊓ U ≤ W ⊓ U := inf_le_inf_right U hle
  rw [resLE_resLE, ← resLE_resLE F (inf_le_left : W ⊓ U ≤ W) h1 t]
  exact germ_appAt inf_le_right h1 (mem_inf hxW' hxU) φ _

end Components

section StalkMap

/-- The component at an open neighbourhood `W` of `x` of the cocone defining `stalkMap`: restrict
a section of `F` over `W` to `W ⊓ U`, apply the component of `φ` there, and take the germ. -/
noncomputable def stalkCoconeApp {U : Opens X} (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) {x : X} (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (W : (OpenNhds x)ᵒᵖ) :
    ((OpenNhds.inclusion x).op ⋙ (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).presheaf).obj W ⟶ modStalk G x :=
  (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left (b := U))).op ≫
    (forget₂ (ModuleCat _) Ab).map (φ.val.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE (inf_le_right
      (a := W.unop.1) (b := U)))))) ≫
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ (commVal (Rc := Rc) G).presheaf (W.unop.1 ⊓ U) x (mem_inf W.unop.2 hxU)

/-- The cocone on the diagram computing `F_x`, with vertex `G_x`, induced by a homomorphism
`φ : F|_U ⟶ G|_U` and a point `x ∈ U`. -/
noncomputable def stalkCocone {U : Opens X} (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) {x : X} (hxU : x ∈ U) :
    Cocone ((OpenNhds.inclusion x).op ⋙ (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).presheaf) where
  pt := modStalk G x
  ι :=
    { app := stalkCoconeApp φ hxU
      naturality := by
        intro W W' f
        ext t
        exact germ_appAt_res_inf f.unop.le W'.unop.2 hxU φ t }

/-- The map on stalks at `x` induced by a homomorphism `φ : F|_U ⟶ G|_U` of `O_U`-modules, for a
point `x ∈ U`. -/
noncomputable def stalkMap {U : Opens X} (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) {x : X} (hxU : x ∈ U) :
    modStalk F x ⟶ modStalk G x :=
  colimit.desc _ (stalkCocone φ hxU)

/-- The defining formula for `stalkMap`, valid for an arbitrary open neighbourhood `W` of `x`. -/
lemma stalkMap_germ_inf {U : Opens X} (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) {x : X} (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (W : Opens X) (hxW : x ∈ W) (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op W)) :
    stalkMap φ hxU (germAt F W x hxW t) =
      germAt G (W ⊓ U) x (mem_inf hxW hxU)
        (appAt (inf_le_right : W ⊓ U ≤ U) φ (resLE F (inf_le_left : W ⊓ U ≤ W) t)) :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (colimit.ι_desc (stalkCocone φ hxU) (op (⟨W, hxW⟩ : OpenNhds x))) t

/-- The germ formula for `stalkMap` over an open `W ≤ U`: the germ of a section `t` is sent to
the germ of `φ` applied to `t`. -/
lemma stalkMap_germ {U : Opens X} (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) {x : X} (hxU : x ∈ U)
    {W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (hxW : x ∈ W) (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op W)) :
    stalkMap φ hxU (germAt F W x hxW t) = germAt G W x hxW (appAt hWU φ t) := by
  rw [stalkMap_germ_inf]
  exact germ_appAt hWU (inf_le_left : W ⊓ U ≤ W) (mem_inf hxW hxU) φ t

/-- Two `O_{X,x}`-linear maps out of the stalk `F_x` agree as soon as they agree on germs. -/
lemma linearMap_ext {x : X} {ψ₁ ψ₂ : modStalk F x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x] modStalk G x}
    (h : ∀ (W : Opens X) (hxW : x ∈ W) (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op W)),
      ψ₁ (germAt F W x hxW t) = ψ₂ (germAt F W x hxW t)) :
    ψ₁ = ψ₂ := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun m ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, t, rfl⟩ := exists_germ_eq F m
  exact h W hxW t

/-- `stalkMap φ hxU` is `O_{X,x}`-linear. -/
lemma stalkMap_smul {U : Opens X} (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) {x : X} (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (r : ringStalk Rc x) (m : modStalk F x) :
    stalkMap φ hxU (r • m) = r • stalkMap φ hxU m := by
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, r₀, rfl⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq Rc.obj r
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, t, rfl⟩ := exists_germ_eq F m
  -- Move both representatives onto the common open `V ⊓ W ⊓ U`.
  have hZV : V ⊓ W ⊓ U ≤ V := le_trans inf_le_left inf_le_left
  have hZW : V ⊓ W ⊓ U ≤ W := le_trans inf_le_left inf_le_right
  have hZU : V ⊓ W ⊓ U ≤ U := inf_le_right
  have hxZ : x ∈ V ⊓ W ⊓ U := ⟨⟨hxV, hxW⟩, hxU⟩
  rw [← TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply Rc.obj (homOfLE hZV) x hxZ r₀,
    ← germAt_resLE F hZW hxZ t, stalkMap_germ φ hxU hZU hxZ (resLE F hZW t),
    ← germAt_smul F hxZ (Rc.obj.map (homOfLE hZV).op r₀) (resLE F hZW t),
    stalkMap_germ φ hxU hZU hxZ, appAt_smul, germAt_smul]

/-- The map on stalks induced by `φ : F|_U ⟶ G|_U`, bundled as an `O_{X,x}`-linear map. -/
noncomputable def stalkLinearMap {U : Opens X} (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) {x : X} (hxU : x ∈ U) :
    modStalk F x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x] modStalk G x where
  toFun := stalkMap φ hxU
  map_add' := map_add _
  map_smul' := stalkMap_smul φ hxU

@[simp]
lemma stalkLinearMap_apply {U : Opens X} (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) {x : X} (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (m : modStalk F x) : stalkLinearMap φ hxU m = stalkMap φ hxU m := rfl

/-- `stalkLinearMap` is additive in the homomorphism. -/
lemma stalkLinearMap_add {U : Opens X} (φ ψ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) {x : X} (hxU : x ∈ U) :
    stalkLinearMap (φ + ψ) hxU = stalkLinearMap φ hxU + stalkLinearMap ψ hxU := by
  refine linearMap_ext fun W hxW t ↦ ?_
  rw [stalkLinearMap_apply, LinearMap.add_apply, stalkLinearMap_apply, stalkLinearMap_apply,
    stalkMap_germ_inf, stalkMap_germ_inf, stalkMap_germ_inf, appAt_add_hom, germAt_add]

/-- Restricting a homomorphism to a smaller open set does not change the induced map on stalks:
this is the compatibility making `stalkLinearMap` descend to the stalk of the internal hom. -/
lemma stalkLinearMap_restrict (H : SheafHom Rc F G) {x : X} {U V : Opens X} (hVU : V ≤ U)
    (hxV : x ∈ V) (s : H.obj.val.obj (op U)) :
    stalkLinearMap (H.sectionsEquiv V (H.obj.val.map (homOfLE hVU).op s)) hxV
      = stalkLinearMap (H.sectionsEquiv U s) (hVU hxV) := by
  refine linearMap_ext fun W hxW t ↦ ?_
  rw [stalkLinearMap_apply, stalkLinearMap_apply, stalkMap_germ_inf, stalkMap_germ_inf]
  -- `H.restrict_natural` identifies the two components over `W ⊓ V`, after which the germs
  -- agree because `W ⊓ V ≤ W ⊓ U`.
  have key : appAt (inf_le_right : W ⊓ V ≤ V)
        (H.sectionsEquiv V (H.obj.val.map (homOfLE hVU).op s)) (resLE F inf_le_left t)
      = appAt ((inf_le_right : W ⊓ V ≤ V).trans hVU) (H.sectionsEquiv U s)
          (resLE F inf_le_left t) :=
    (H.restrict_natural hVU s (inf_le_right : W ⊓ V ≤ V) (resLE F inf_le_left t)).symm
  rw [key]
  have h1 : W ⊓ V ≤ W ⊓ U := inf_le_inf_left W hVU
  rw [show resLE F (inf_le_left : W ⊓ V ≤ W) t
      = resLE F h1 (resLE F (inf_le_left : W ⊓ U ≤ W) t) from (resLE_resLE F _ h1 t).symm]
  exact germ_appAt (inf_le_right : W ⊓ U ≤ U) h1 (mem_inf hxW hxV) (H.sectionsEquiv U s) _

end StalkMap

section SheafHomStalk

/-- The component at an open neighbourhood `U` of `x` of the cocone defining
`sheafHomStalkLinearMap`: a section of the internal hom over `U` is a homomorphism
`F|_U ⟶ G|_U`, which induces an `O_{X,x}`-linear map `F_x →ₗ G_x`. -/
noncomputable def sheafHomCoconeApp (H : SheafHom Rc F G) {x : X} (U : (OpenNhds x)ᵒᵖ) :
    ((OpenNhds.inclusion x).op ⋙ (commVal (Rc := Rc) H.obj).presheaf).obj U ⟶
      AddCommGrpCat.of (modStalk F x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x] modStalk G x) :=
  AddCommGrpCat.ofHom (AddMonoidHom.mk'
    (fun s ↦ stalkLinearMap (H.sectionsEquiv U.unop.1 s) U.unop.2)
    (fun s s' ↦ (congrArg (fun φ ↦ stalkLinearMap φ U.unop.2)
      ((H.sectionsEquiv U.unop.1).map_add s s')).trans (stalkLinearMap_add _ _ U.unop.2)))

/-- The cocone on the diagram computing the stalk of the internal hom, with vertex the module of
`O_{X,x}`-linear maps `F_x →ₗ G_x`. -/
noncomputable def sheafHomCocone (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X) :
    Cocone ((OpenNhds.inclusion x).op ⋙ (commVal (Rc := Rc) H.obj).presheaf) where
  pt := AddCommGrpCat.of (modStalk F x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x] modStalk G x)
  ι :=
    { app := sheafHomCoconeApp H
      naturality := by
        intro U V f
        ext s
        exact stalkLinearMap_restrict H f.unop.le V.unop.2 s }

/-- The canonical additive map from the stalk at `x` of the internal hom
`SheafHom_{O_X}(F, G)` to the module of `O_{X,x}`-linear maps `F_x →ₗ G_x`. -/
noncomputable def sheafHomStalkMap (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X) :
    modStalk H.obj x ⟶ AddCommGrpCat.of (modStalk F x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x] modStalk G x) :=
  colimit.desc _ (sheafHomCocone H x)

/-- The canonical map sends the germ of a local homomorphism to the induced map on stalks. -/
lemma sheafHomStalkMap_germ (H : SheafHom Rc F G) {x : X} (U : Opens X) (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (s : H.obj.val.obj (op U)) :
    sheafHomStalkMap H x (germAt H.obj U x hxU s) = stalkLinearMap (H.sectionsEquiv U s) hxU :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (colimit.ι_desc (sheafHomCocone H x) (op (⟨U, hxU⟩ : OpenNhds x))) s

/-- The canonical map is `O_{X,x}`-linear. -/
lemma sheafHomStalkMap_smul (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X) (r : ringStalk Rc x)
    (σ : modStalk H.obj x) :
    sheafHomStalkMap H x (r • σ) = r • sheafHomStalkMap H x σ := by
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, r₀, rfl⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq Rc.obj r
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, s, rfl⟩ := exists_germ_eq H.obj σ
  have hZV : V ⊓ U ≤ V := inf_le_left
  have hZU : V ⊓ U ≤ U := inf_le_right
  have hxZ : x ∈ V ⊓ U := ⟨hxV, hxU⟩
  rw [← TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply Rc.obj (homOfLE hZV) x hxZ r₀,
    ← germAt_resLE H.obj hZU hxZ s, sheafHomStalkMap_germ H (V ⊓ U) hxZ (resLE H.obj hZU s),
    ← germAt_smul H.obj hxZ (Rc.obj.map (homOfLE hZV).op r₀) (resLE H.obj hZU s),
    sheafHomStalkMap_germ H (V ⊓ U) hxZ]
  -- Compare the two `O_{X,x}`-linear maps on germs, using `H.smul_natural`.
  refine linearMap_ext fun W hxW t ↦ ?_
  rw [stalkLinearMap_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, stalkLinearMap_apply,
    stalkMap_germ_inf, stalkMap_germ_inf]
  have key := H.smul_natural (V ⊓ U) (Rc.obj.map (homOfLE hZV).op r₀) (resLE H.obj hZU s)
    (inf_le_right : W ⊓ (V ⊓ U) ≤ V ⊓ U) (resLE F inf_le_left t)
  rw [show appAt (inf_le_right : W ⊓ (V ⊓ U) ≤ V ⊓ U)
        (H.sectionsEquiv (V ⊓ U) (Rc.obj.map (homOfLE hZV).op r₀ • resLE H.obj hZU s))
        (resLE F inf_le_left t)
      = Rc.obj.map (homOfLE (inf_le_right : W ⊓ (V ⊓ U) ≤ V ⊓ U)).op
          (Rc.obj.map (homOfLE hZV).op r₀) •
        appAt (inf_le_right : W ⊓ (V ⊓ U) ≤ V ⊓ U) (H.sectionsEquiv (V ⊓ U) (resLE H.obj hZU s))
          (resLE F inf_le_left t) from key,
    germAt_smul, ← TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply Rc.obj
      (homOfLE (inf_le_right : W ⊓ (V ⊓ U) ≤ V ⊓ U)) x (mem_inf hxW hxZ)]

/-- **The canonical map of Stacks 01CP.** The `O_{X,x}`-linear map from the stalk at `x` of the
internal hom `SheafHom_{O_X}(F, G)` to the module of `O_{X,x}`-linear maps `F_x →ₗ G_x`, sending
the germ of a local homomorphism to the induced map on stalks. -/
noncomputable def sheafHomStalkLinearMap (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X) :
    modStalk H.obj x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x]
      (modStalk F x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x] modStalk G x) where
  toFun := sheafHomStalkMap H x
  map_add' := map_add _
  map_smul' := sheafHomStalkMap_smul H x

/-- The germ formula characterizing the canonical map: the germ of a local homomorphism `s` and
the germ of a local section `t`, both taken over the same open `U`, are sent to the germ of the
evaluation of `s` on `t`. -/
lemma sheafHomStalkLinearMap_germ (H : SheafHom Rc F G) {x : X} (U : Opens X) (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (s : H.obj.val.obj (op U)) (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op U)) :
    sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x (germAt H.obj U x hxU s) (germAt F U x hxU t)
      = germAt G U x hxU (appAt le_rfl (H.sectionsEquiv U s) t) := by
  change sheafHomStalkMap H x (germAt H.obj U x hxU s) (germAt F U x hxU t) = _
  rw [sheafHomStalkMap_germ H U hxU s, stalkLinearMap_apply,
    stalkMap_germ (H.sectionsEquiv U s) hxU le_rfl hxU t]

/-- The germ formula pins down the canonical map: any `O_{X,x}`-linear map out of the stalk of
the internal hom which satisfies it is equal to `sheafHomStalkLinearMap`. -/
lemma sheafHomStalkLinearMap_unique (H : SheafHom Rc F G) {x : X}
    (Φ : modStalk H.obj x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x]
      (modStalk F x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x] modStalk G x))
    (hΦ : ∀ (U : Opens X) (hxU : x ∈ U) (s : H.obj.val.obj (op U))
      (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op U)),
      Φ (germAt H.obj U x hxU s) (germAt F U x hxU t)
        = germAt G U x hxU (appAt le_rfl (H.sectionsEquiv U s) t)) :
    Φ = sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun σ ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, s, rfl⟩ := exists_germ_eq H.obj σ
  refine LinearMap.ext fun m ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, t, rfl⟩ := exists_germ_eq F m
  -- Bring the two germs onto the common open `W ⊓ U`.
  have hZU : W ⊓ U ≤ U := inf_le_right
  have hZW : W ⊓ U ≤ W := inf_le_left
  have hxZ : x ∈ W ⊓ U := ⟨hxW, hxU⟩
  rw [← germAt_resLE H.obj hZU hxZ s, ← germAt_resLE F hZW hxZ t, hΦ (W ⊓ U) hxZ _ _,
    sheafHomStalkLinearMap_germ H (W ⊓ U) hxZ]

/-- The component at `U` of a homomorphism of `O_U`-modules, written with the identity of `U`
rather than `homOfLE le_rfl`. -/
lemma app_id {U : Opens X} (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) (t : (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op U)) :
    φ.val.app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 U))) t = appAt le_rfl φ t := rfl

end SheafHomStalk

section Equiv

/-- A canonical linear equivalence from the stalk of the internal hom `SheafHom_{O_X}(F, G)` to
the module of `O_{X,x}`-linear maps `F_x →ₗ G_x`. The second field specifies the equivalence on
germs, which by `sheafHomStalkLinearMap_unique` forces it to be the canonical map
`sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x`; so this structure asserts that *the canonical map* is an
isomorphism, not merely that its source and target are isomorphic. -/
structure SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv (Rc : TopCat.Sheaf CommRingCat.{v} X)
    (F G : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X) where
  /-- The isomorphism from the stalk of the internal hom to the module of linear maps between
  the stalks. -/
  equiv : modStalk H.obj x ≃ₗ[ringStalk Rc x]
    (modStalk F x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x] modStalk G x)
  /-- On germs, the equivalence is evaluation of the represented local homomorphism on the
  represented local section. -/
  germ_apply (U : Opens X) (hxU : x ∈ U) (s : H.obj.val.obj (op U))
      (m : (commVal F).obj (op U)) :
    equiv (germAt H.obj U x hxU s) (germAt F U x hxU m)
      = germAt G U x hxU ((H.sectionsEquiv U s).val.app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 U))) m)

namespace SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv

variable {H : SheafHom Rc F G} {x : X}

/-- The underlying linear map of a `SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv` is the canonical map. -/
lemma toLinearMap_eq (E : SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv Rc F G H x) :
    (E.equiv : modStalk H.obj x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x]
      (modStalk F x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x] modStalk G x)) = sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x :=
  sheafHomStalkLinearMap_unique H _ (fun U hxU s m ↦ E.germ_apply U hxU s m)

/-- If the canonical map admits a `SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv`, then the canonical map itself is
bijective. -/
lemma bijective (E : SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv Rc F G H x) :
    Function.Bijective (sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x) := by
  have key : ∀ m, sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x m = E.equiv m :=
    fun m ↦ (LinearMap.congr_fun E.toLinearMap_eq m).symm
  refine ⟨fun a b hab ↦ E.equiv.injective ?_, fun y ↦ ?_⟩
  · rw [← key, ← key, hab]
  · obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := E.equiv.surjective y
    exact ⟨a, by rw [key, ha]⟩

/-- Conversely, bijectivity of the canonical map produces a `SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv`. Together
with `SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv.bijective` this reduces Stacks 01CP to the statement that the
canonical map `sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x` is bijective. -/
noncomputable def ofBijective (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X)
    (hb : Function.Bijective (sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x)) :
    SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv Rc F G H x where
  equiv := LinearEquiv.ofBijective (sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x) hb
  germ_apply U hxU s m := by
    change sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x (germAt H.obj U x hxU s) (germAt F U x hxU m) = _
    rw [sheafHomStalkLinearMap_germ H U hxU s m, app_id]

end SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv

end Equiv

section FinitePresentation

/-!
### Bijectivity of the canonical map for a finitely presented module

The section-level finite-presentation data is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalPresentation`, obtained
from `SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation` by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_localPresentation`.
Its vocabulary (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.res`, `resR`, `germ`) spells scalars in
`(structureSheaf Rc).obj`, i.e. in `RingCat`, whereas the module structure on `modStalk` needs
them in `Rc.obj`, i.e. in `CommRingCat`. The two carriers are identical and the two `Module`
instances are literally the same term, so the crossing is definitional; `germAt_smul_ring` is the
one bridge where it is performed, and `resLE_eq_res`/`germAt_eq_germ` are the (`rfl`) translations
between the two spellings of restriction and germ.
-/

open Stacks.SheafOfModules in
/-- The `≤`-indexed restriction of this file is `StalkFreeCover`'s hom-indexed one. -/
lemma resLE_eq_res (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W W' : Opens X}
    (h : W' ≤ W) (t : (commVal M).obj (op W)) :
    resLE M h t = res M (homOfLE h) t := rfl

open Stacks.SheafOfModules in
/-- The germ of this file is `StalkFreeCover`'s germ. -/
lemma germAt_eq_germ (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) (W : Opens X) (x : X)
    (hx : x ∈ W) (t : (commVal M).obj (op W)) :
    germAt M W x hx t = germ M x hx t := rfl

/-- `germAt_smul` with the scalar spelled in `(structureSheaf Rc).obj`, which is the spelling
produced by `StalkFreeCover`'s section-level lemmas. The conclusion still uses the `CommRingCat`
stalk, because that is the ring `modStalk` is a module over. -/
lemma germAt_smul_ring (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W : Opens X} {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ W) (a : (structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj (op W)) (t : M.val.obj (op W)) :
    germAt M W x hx (a • t)
      = TopCat.Presheaf.germ (C := CommRingCat.{v}) Rc.obj W x hx a • germAt M W x hx t :=
  PresheafOfModules.germ_smul (commVal M) x W hx a t

lemma germAt_sum (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W : Opens X} {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ W) {ι : Type*} (u : Finset ι) (m : ι → (commVal M).obj (op W)) :
    germAt M W x hx (∑ i ∈ u, m i) = ∑ i ∈ u, germAt M W x hx (m i) :=
  map_sum (TopCat.Presheaf.germ (C := Ab.{v}) (commVal M).presheaf W x hx).hom m u

open Stacks.SheafOfModules in
/-- A section of a sheaf of modules which vanishes locally vanishes. This is the module-level
counterpart of `StalkFreeCover`'s `eq_zero_of_locally_zero`, which is stated for the structure
sheaf. -/
lemma eq_zero_of_locally_zero_mod (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {V : Opens X}
    (m : M.val.obj (op V))
    (hm : ∀ y ∈ V, ∃ (W : Opens X) (h : W ⟶ V), y ∈ W ∧ res M h m = 0) : m = 0 := by
  refine TopCat.Presheaf.section_ext
    ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf (structureSheaf Rc)).obj M) V m 0 fun y hy ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨W, h, hyW, h0⟩ := hm y hy
  calc TopCat.Presheaf.germ (C := Ab.{v}) (commVal M).presheaf V y hy m
      = germAt M W y hyW (resLE M h.le m) := (germAt_resLE M h.le hyW m).symm
    _ = germAt M W y hyW 0 := by rw [resLE_eq_res]; exact congrArg _ h0
    _ = 0 := germAt_zero M hyW
    _ = TopCat.Presheaf.germ (C := Ab.{v}) (commVal M).presheaf V y hy 0 :=
        (germAt_zero M hy).symm

/-- A morphism of sheaves of modules all of whose components vanish on all sections is zero. -/
lemma hom_eq_zero_of_app_eq_zero {C' : Type u'} [Category.{v} C']
    {J' : GrothendieckTopology C'} {S : CategoryTheory.Sheaf J' RingCat.{v}}
    {A B : SheafOfModules.{v} S} (ψ : A ⟶ B)
    (h : ∀ (Z : C'ᵒᵖ) (t : A.val.obj Z), ψ.val.app Z t = 0) : ψ = 0 := by
  ext Z t
  rw [h Z t]
  exact (Stacks.SheafOfModules.zero_app_apply Z t).symm

section LocalPresentationStalk

open Stacks.SheafOfModules

lemma resLE_zero (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W W' : Opens X} (h : W' ≤ W) :
    resLE M h (0 : (commVal M).obj (op W)) = 0 := map_zero _

/-- Normalise a restriction along an arbitrary hom of opens to the `≤`-indexed one. -/
lemma res_eq_resLE (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W W' : Opens X}
    (f : W' ⟶ W) (t : (commVal M).obj (op W)) : res M f t = resLE M f.le t :=
  M.val.congr_map_apply (Subsingleton.elim _ _) t

/-- Restriction along two (necessarily equal) inclusions of opens agrees. -/
private lemma res_eq_res_aux (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W W' : Opens X}
    (f f' : W' ⟶ W) (m : (commVal M).obj (op W)) : res M f m = res M f' m :=
  (res_eq_resLE M f m).trans (res_eq_resLE M f' m).symm

/-- Normalise a restriction of the structure sheaf along an arbitrary hom of opens. -/
lemma resR_eq_resRLE {W W' : Opens X} (f f' : W' ⟶ W)
    (a : (structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj (op W)) :
    resR (structureSheaf Rc) f a = resR (structureSheaf Rc) f' a :=
  congrArg (fun h ↦ (structureSheaf Rc).obj.map h a) (Subsingleton.elim _ _)

/-- The component of `φ` at `W ≤ U` with source and target spelled through `M.val`, so that the
scalars are the `(structureSheaf Rc)`-spelled ones that `StalkFreeCover`'s section-level lemmas
produce. This is the same function as `appAt` (`appAtR_eq_appAt` is `rfl`); the duplication is
forced, not chosen, because the `Rc.obj`-module structure and the
`(structureSheaf Rc).obj`-module structure on a group of sections are definitionally the same
term but are each found by instance search only at their own spelling. `appAt` carries the
`Rc.obj` spelling, which is what the stalk's module structure needs; `appAtR` carries the
`RingCat` spelling, which is what the local-presentation data speaks. -/
noncomputable def appAtR {U W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U)
    (t : F.val.obj (op W)) : G.val.obj (op W) :=
  φ.val.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hWU))) t

lemma appAtR_eq_appAt {U W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U)
    (t : F.val.obj (op W)) : appAtR hWU φ t = appAt hWU φ t := rfl

lemma appAtR_smul {U W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U)
    (r : (structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj (op W)) (t : F.val.obj (op W)) :
    appAtR hWU φ (r • t) = r • appAtR hWU φ t :=
  appAt_smul hWU φ r t

lemma appAtR_zero {U W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) :
    appAtR hWU φ (0 : F.val.obj (op W)) = 0 := appAt_zero hWU φ

lemma appAtR_sum {U W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) {ι : Type*}
    (u : Finset ι) (m : ι → F.val.obj (op W)) :
    appAtR hWU φ (∑ i ∈ u, m i) = ∑ i ∈ u, appAtR hWU φ (m i) :=
  map_sum (φ.val.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE hWU)))).hom m u

lemma appAt_sum {U W : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) {ι : Type*}
    (u : Finset ι) (m : ι → (commVal (Rc := Rc) F).obj (op W)) :
    appAt hWU φ (∑ i ∈ u, m i) = ∑ i ∈ u, appAt hWU φ (m i) :=
  appAtR_sum hWU φ u m

variable {x : X}

/-- The germs at `x` of the generators of a local presentation span the stalk. -/
lemma exists_coeffs_germAt (LP : LocalPresentation F x) (m : modStalk F x) :
    ∃ c : LP.Gen → ringStalk Rc x,
      m = ∑ k : LP.Gen, c k • germAt F LP.nhd x LP.mem_nhd (LP.gens k) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, t, rfl⟩ := exists_germ_eq F m
  obtain ⟨W', g, hxW', c, hc⟩ :=
    LP.generates (homOfLE (inf_le_right : W ⊓ LP.nhd ≤ LP.nhd))
      (resLE F inf_le_left t) x (mem_inf hxW LP.mem_nhd)
  refine ⟨fun k ↦ TopCat.Presheaf.germ (C := CommRingCat.{v}) Rc.obj W' x hxW' (c k), ?_⟩
  rw [res_eq_resLE] at hc
  calc germAt F W x hxW t
      = germAt F W' x hxW'
          (resLE F g.le (resLE F (inf_le_left : W ⊓ LP.nhd ≤ W) t)) := by
        rw [germAt_resLE, germAt_resLE]
    _ = germAt F W' x hxW'
          (∑ k : LP.Gen, c k • res F (g ≫ homOfLE inf_le_right) (LP.gens k)) := by rw [hc]
    _ = ∑ k : LP.Gen, TopCat.Presheaf.germ (C := CommRingCat.{v}) Rc.obj W' x hxW' (c k)
          • germAt F LP.nhd x LP.mem_nhd (LP.gens k) := by
        rw [germAt_sum]
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ ↦ ?_
        rw [res_eq_resLE, germAt_smul_ring, germAt_resLE]

/-- Two linear maps out of the stalk agree as soon as they agree on the germs of the generators
of a local presentation. -/
lemma linearMap_ext_gens (LP : LocalPresentation F x)
    {ψ₁ ψ₂ : modStalk F x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x] modStalk G x}
    (h : ∀ k : LP.Gen, ψ₁ (germAt F LP.nhd x LP.mem_nhd (LP.gens k))
      = ψ₂ (germAt F LP.nhd x LP.mem_nhd (LP.gens k))) : ψ₁ = ψ₂ := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun m ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := exists_coeffs_germAt LP m
  simp only [map_sum, map_smul, h]

/-- `appAtR` is natural in the open set. -/
lemma appAtR_res {U W W' : Opens X} (hWU : W ≤ U) (hW'W : W' ≤ W)
    (φ : F.over U ⟶ G.over U) (t : F.val.obj (op W)) :
    appAtR (hW'W.trans hWU) φ (res F (homOfLE hW'W) t)
      = res G (homOfLE hW'W) (appAtR hWU φ t) :=
  appAt_res hWU hW'W φ t

/-- If the components of `φ` annihilate the restricted generators on a neighbourhood `V₁`, then
`φ` annihilates every section over every open contained in `V₁`. This is the local-generation
step of the injectivity half of Stacks 01CP. -/
lemma appAtR_eq_zero_of_gens (LP : LocalGenerators F x) {V₀ : Opens X} (hV₀U : V₀ ≤ LP.nhd)
    (φ : F.over V₀ ⟶ G.over V₀) {V₁ : Opens X} (hV₁ : V₁ ≤ V₀)
    (hgens : ∀ k : LP.Gen,
      res G (homOfLE hV₁) (appAtR le_rfl φ (res F (homOfLE hV₀U) (LP.gens k))) = 0)
    {W : Opens X} (hWV₁ : W ≤ V₁) (t : F.val.obj (op W)) :
    appAtR (hWV₁.trans hV₁) φ t = 0 := by
  classical
  have hzero : ∀ (k : LP.Gen) {W' : Opens X} (hW' : W' ≤ V₁),
      appAtR (hW'.trans hV₁) φ (res F (homOfLE (hW'.trans (hV₁.trans hV₀U))) (LP.gens k)) = 0 := by
    intro k W' hW'
    have e1 : res F (homOfLE (hW'.trans (hV₁.trans hV₀U))) (LP.gens k)
        = res F (homOfLE hW') (res F (homOfLE hV₁) (res F (homOfLE hV₀U) (LP.gens k))) := by
      rw [res_res, res_res]
      exact res_eq_res_aux F _ _ _
    rw [e1, appAtR_res hV₁ hW' φ _, appAtR_res le_rfl hV₁ φ _, hgens k, res_zero]
  refine eq_zero_of_locally_zero_mod G _ fun y hy ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨W', g, hyW', c, hc⟩ :=
    LP.generates (homOfLE ((hWV₁.trans hV₁).trans hV₀U)) t y hy
  refine ⟨W', g, hyW', ?_⟩
  rw [res_eq_resLE, resLE_eq_res] at hc ⊢
  rw [← appAtR_res (hWV₁.trans hV₁) g.le φ t, hc, appAtR_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun k _ ↦ ?_
  have h0 : appAtR (g.le.trans (hWV₁.trans hV₁)) φ
      (res F (g ≫ homOfLE ((hWV₁.trans hV₁).trans hV₀U)) (LP.gens k)) = 0 := by
    rw [res_eq_resLE, resLE_eq_res]
    exact hzero k (g.le.trans hWV₁)
  rw [appAtR_smul, h0, smul_zero]

/-- Every object of the slice site over an open `U` is the one determined by the inclusion
underlying its structure map. -/
lemma op_over_eq {U : Opens X} (Z : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) :
    Z = op (Over.mk (homOfLE Z.unop.hom.le)) :=
  congrArg op (congrArg Over.mk (Subsingleton.elim _ _))

/-- **Injectivity half of Stacks 01CP, from local generators at `x`.** The canonical map from the
stalk of the internal hom to the module of homomorphisms of the stalks is injective as soon as
`F` is generated, on *some* neighbourhood of `x`, by finitely many sections — which is exactly a
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalGenerators F x`. Nothing is assumed about `F` away from that
neighbourhood.

`injective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap` is the global-hypothesis form, obtained by producing the local
generators from `F` being of finite type. This germ-local form is what a statement about a single
stalk needs, and the only hypothesis the argument below ever uses. -/
theorem injective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localGenerators (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X)
    (LP : LocalGenerators F x) : Function.Injective (sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x) := by
  classical
  refine (injective_iff_map_eq_zero (sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x)).mpr fun σ hσ ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, s, rfl⟩ := exists_germ_eq H.obj σ
  have hV₀V : V ⊓ LP.nhd ≤ V := inf_le_left
  have hV₀U : V ⊓ LP.nhd ≤ LP.nhd := inf_le_right
  have hxV₀ : x ∈ V ⊓ LP.nhd := mem_inf hxV LP.mem_nhd
  have hgerm : germAt H.obj (V ⊓ LP.nhd) x hxV₀ (resLE H.obj hV₀V s)
      = germAt H.obj V x hxV s := germAt_resLE _ _ _ _
  set φ := H.sectionsEquiv (V ⊓ LP.nhd) (resLE H.obj hV₀V s)
  have hzeroφ : stalkLinearMap φ hxV₀ = 0 := by
    rw [← sheafHomStalkMap_germ H (V ⊓ LP.nhd) hxV₀ (resLE H.obj hV₀V s)]
    change sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x
      (germAt H.obj (V ⊓ LP.nhd) x hxV₀ (resLE H.obj hV₀V s)) = 0
    rw [hgerm]
    exact hσ
  have hk : ∀ k : LP.Gen, ∃ (W : Opens X) (h : W ⟶ V ⊓ LP.nhd), x ∈ W ∧
      res G h (appAtR le_rfl φ (res F (homOfLE hV₀U) (LP.gens k))) = 0 := by
    intro k
    have h1 : germ G x hxV₀ (appAtR le_rfl φ (res F (homOfLE hV₀U) (LP.gens k)))
        = germ G x hxV₀ (0 : G.val.obj (op (V ⊓ LP.nhd))) := by
      have h2 := LinearMap.congr_fun hzeroφ
        (germAt F (V ⊓ LP.nhd) x hxV₀ (res F (homOfLE hV₀U) (LP.gens k)))
      rw [stalkLinearMap_apply, LinearMap.zero_apply,
        stalkMap_germ φ hxV₀ le_rfl hxV₀ (res F (homOfLE hV₀U) (LP.gens k))] at h2
      rw [← germAt_eq_germ, ← germAt_eq_germ, appAtR_eq_appAt, germAt_zero]
      exact h2
    obtain ⟨W, h, hxW, hres⟩ := exists_res_eq x hxV₀ _ _ h1
    exact ⟨W, h, hxW, by rw [hres, res_zero]⟩
  choose W hWhom hxW hres using hk
  obtain ⟨V₁, fV₁, hxV₁, hV₁W⟩ := exists_nbhd_le' x (V ⊓ LP.nhd) hxV₀ W hxW
  have hgens : ∀ k : LP.Gen,
      res G (homOfLE fV₁.le) (appAtR le_rfl φ (res F (homOfLE hV₀U) (LP.gens k))) = 0 := by
    intro k
    rw [res_eq_res_aux G _ (homOfLE (hV₁W k) ≫ hWhom k), ← res_res, hres k, res_zero]
  have hmorph : H.sectionsEquiv V₁
      (H.obj.val.map (homOfLE fV₁.le).op (resLE H.obj hV₀V s)) = 0 := by
    refine hom_eq_zero_of_app_eq_zero _ fun Z t ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨⟨Wz, _rz, fz⟩⟩ := Z
    change (H.sectionsEquiv V₁
      (H.obj.val.map (homOfLE fV₁.le).op (resLE H.obj hV₀V s))).val.app
      (op (Over.mk (homOfLE fz.le))) t = 0
    rw [← H.restrict_natural fV₁.le (resLE H.obj hV₀V s) fz.le t]
    exact appAtR_eq_zero_of_gens LP hV₀U _ fV₁.le hgens fz.le t
  have hs0 : resLE H.obj fV₁.le (resLE H.obj hV₀V s) = 0 := by
    refine (H.sectionsEquiv V₁).injective ?_
    rw [map_zero]
    exact hmorph
  calc germAt H.obj V x hxV s
      = germAt H.obj (V ⊓ LP.nhd) x hxV₀ (resLE H.obj hV₀V s) := hgerm.symm
    _ = germAt H.obj V₁ x hxV₁ (resLE H.obj fV₁.le (resLE H.obj hV₀V s)) :=
        (germAt_resLE H.obj fV₁.le hxV₁ (resLE H.obj hV₀V s)).symm
    _ = 0 := by rw [hs0]; exact germAt_zero _ _

/-- **Injectivity half of Stacks 01CP.** For `F` of finite type the canonical map from the stalk
of the internal hom to the module of homomorphisms of the stalks is injective. Only local
generation by finitely many sections is used, which is exactly `LocalGenerators`; the relations
of a `LocalPresentation` are needed only for surjectivity.

This is `injective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localGenerators`, whose hypothesis is only that `F`
has local generators at `x`, applied to the generators that finite type produces there. -/
@[stacks 01CP "finite_type_injective", ega "0 5.2.6" "partial"]
theorem injective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X)
    [F.IsFiniteType] : Function.Injective (sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x) :=
  (nonempty_localGenerators F x).elim
    (injective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localGenerators H x)

/-- The germ of a restricted section of the structure sheaf, in the `CommRingCat` stalk that the
module structure on `modStalk` uses. -/
lemma germR_resR {U V : Opens X} (f : V ⟶ U) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ V)
    (a : (structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj (op U)) :
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ (C := CommRingCat.{v}) Rc.obj V x hx (resR (structureSheaf Rc) f a)
      = TopCat.Presheaf.germ (C := CommRingCat.{v}) Rc.obj U x (f.le hx) a :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply Rc.obj (homOfLE f.le) x hx a

/-- Realise a prospective homomorphism of stalks on the generators of a local presentation:
there is a neighbourhood of `x` carrying sections `g k` whose germs are the values of `ψ` on the
germs of the generators, and which satisfy every relation of the presentation. -/
lemma exists_gens_images (LP : LocalPresentation F x)
    (ψ : modStalk F x →ₗ[ringStalk Rc x] modStalk G x) :
    ∃ (V : Opens X) (fV : V ⟶ LP.nhd) (hxV : x ∈ V) (g : LP.Gen → G.val.obj (op V)),
      (∀ k, germAt G V x hxV (g k) = ψ (germAt F LP.nhd x LP.mem_nhd (LP.gens k))) ∧
      (∀ l, ∑ k : LP.Gen, resR (structureSheaf Rc) fV (LP.rel l k) • g k = 0) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, gk, hgk⟩ : ∃ (W : LP.Gen → Opens X) (hxW : ∀ k, x ∈ W k)
      (gk : ∀ k, G.val.obj (op (W k))),
      ∀ k, germAt G (W k) x (hxW k) (gk k)
        = ψ (germAt F LP.nhd x LP.mem_nhd (LP.gens k)) := by
    choose W hxW gk hgk using fun k : LP.Gen ↦
      exists_germ_eq G (ψ (germAt F LP.nhd x LP.mem_nhd (LP.gens k)))
    exact ⟨W, hxW, gk, hgk⟩
  obtain ⟨V, fV, hxV, hVW⟩ := exists_nbhd_le' x LP.nhd LP.mem_nhd W hxW
  have hg : ∀ k, germAt G V x hxV (res G (homOfLE (hVW k)) (gk k))
      = ψ (germAt F LP.nhd x LP.mem_nhd (LP.gens k)) := by
    intro k
    rw [← resLE_eq_res, germAt_resLE]
    exact hgk k
  have h2 : ∀ l : LP.Rel,
      germ G x hxV (∑ k : LP.Gen, resR (structureSheaf Rc) fV (LP.rel l k)
        • res G (homOfLE (hVW k)) (gk k)) = germ G x hxV (0 : G.val.obj (op V)) := by
    intro l
    rw [← germAt_eq_germ, ← germAt_eq_germ, germAt_zero, germAt_sum]
    calc ∑ k : LP.Gen, germAt G V x hxV (resR (structureSheaf Rc) fV (LP.rel l k)
            • res G (homOfLE (hVW k)) (gk k))
        = ∑ k : LP.Gen, TopCat.Presheaf.germ (C := CommRingCat.{v}) Rc.obj LP.nhd x LP.mem_nhd
            (LP.rel l k) • ψ (germAt F LP.nhd x LP.mem_nhd (LP.gens k)) := by
          refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ ↦ ?_
          rw [germAt_smul_ring, germR_resR, hg k]
      _ = ψ (germAt F LP.nhd x LP.mem_nhd (∑ k : LP.Gen, LP.rel l k • LP.gens k)) := by
          rw [germAt_sum, map_sum]
          refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ ↦ ?_
          rw [germAt_smul_ring, map_smul]
      _ = 0 := by rw [LP.rel_apply l, germAt_zero, map_zero]
  choose W' hW'hom hxW' hW'zero using fun l ↦ exists_res_eq x hxV _ _ (h2 l)
  obtain ⟨V', fV', hxV', hV'W'⟩ := exists_nbhd_le' x V hxV W' hxW'
  refine ⟨V', fV' ≫ fV, hxV', fun k ↦ res G fV' (res G (homOfLE (hVW k)) (gk k)),
    fun k ↦ ?_, fun l ↦ ?_⟩
  · dsimp only
    rw [res_eq_resLE, germAt_resLE]
    exact hg k
  · have e : res G (homOfLE (hV'W' l) ≫ hW'hom l)
          (∑ k : LP.Gen, resR (structureSheaf Rc) fV (LP.rel l k)
            • res G (homOfLE (hVW k)) (gk k)) = 0 := by
      rw [← res_res, hW'zero l, res_zero, res_zero]
    rw [res_sum_smul] at e
    dsimp only
    refine Eq.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ ↦ ?_) e
    have hs : resR (structureSheaf Rc) (fV' ≫ fV) (LP.rel l k)
        = resR (structureSheaf Rc) (homOfLE (hV'W' l) ≫ hW'hom l)
            (resR (structureSheaf Rc) fV (LP.rel l k)) := by
      rw [resR_resR]
      exact resR_eq_resRLE _ _ _
    have hm : res G fV' (res G (homOfLE (hVW k)) (gk k))
        = res G (homOfLE (hV'W' l) ≫ hW'hom l) (res G (homOfLE (hVW k)) (gk k)) :=
      res_eq_res_aux G _ _ _
    rw [hs, hm]

/-- Restriction along two (necessarily equal) inclusions of opens agrees. -/
lemma res_eq_res (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) {W W' : Opens X}
    (f f' : W' ⟶ W) (m : (commVal M).obj (op W)) : res M f m = res M f' m :=
  res_eq_res_aux M f f' m

/-- If each coefficient `z k` is a combination `∑ l, b l * A l k` of relation coefficients, and
each relation `∑ k, A l k • m k` vanishes, then `∑ k, z k • m k` vanishes. Pure algebra, used to
regroup a double sum. -/
lemma sum_smul_eq_zero_of_relations {Rr : Type*} [Ring Rr] {Mm : Type*} [AddCommGroup Mm]
    [Module Rr Mm] {ι κ : Type*} [Fintype ι] [Fintype κ]
    (z : κ → Rr) (b : ι → Rr) (A : ι → κ → Rr) (m : κ → Mm)
    (hz : ∀ k, z k = ∑ l : ι, b l * A l k)
    (hA : ∀ l, ∑ k : κ, A l k • m k = 0) :
    ∑ k : κ, z k • m k = 0 := by
  have hreg : ∑ k : κ, z k • m k = ∑ l : ι, b l • ∑ k : κ, A l k • m k := by
    simp only [hz, Finset.sum_smul, Finset.smul_sum, mul_smul]
    exact Finset.sum_comm
  rw [hreg]
  exact Finset.sum_eq_zero fun l _ ↦ by rw [hA l, smul_zero]

/-- An epimorphism out of a free module whose kernel is annihilated by a second map out of the
same free module factors that second map. This is the only place where the abelian structure of
`SheafOfModules` is used: an epimorphism is the cokernel of its kernel. -/
lemma exists_factor_of_epi {V : Opens X} {ι : Type v}
    (π : SheafOfModules.free (R := (structureSheaf Rc).over V) ι ⟶ F.over V) [Epi π]
    (β : SheafOfModules.free (R := (structureSheaf Rc).over V) ι ⟶ G.over V)
    (hκ : kernel.ι π ≫ β = 0) :
    ∃ φ : F.over V ⟶ G.over V, π ≫ φ = β :=
  let hck : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ π (kernel.condition π)) :=
    Abelian.epiIsCokernelOfKernel _ (limit.isLimit _)
  ⟨(CokernelCofork.IsColimit.desc' hck β hκ).1, (CokernelCofork.IsColimit.desc' hck β hκ).2⟩

/-- Sections of `G` satisfying every relation of a local presentation of `F` define a
homomorphism `F|_V ⟶ G|_V`: the presentation exhibits `F|_V` as the cokernel of a map of finite
free modules, and the relations say exactly that the prospective map kills that kernel. -/
lemma exists_hom_of_rel_zero (LP : LocalPresentation F x) {V : Opens X} (fV : V ⟶ LP.nhd)
    (g : LP.Gen → G.val.obj (op V))
    (hrel : ∀ l : LP.Rel,
      ∑ k : LP.Gen, resR (structureSheaf Rc) fV (LP.rel l k) • g k = 0) :
    ∃ φ : F.over V ⟶ G.over V, ∀ k, appAtR le_rfl φ (res F fV (LP.gens k)) = g k := by
  classical
  have hepi : Epi (freeToOver F (fun k ↦ res F fV (LP.gens k))) := by
    refine epi_freeToOver F _ fun {W} f t y hy ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨W', h, hyW', c, hc⟩ := LP.generates (f ≫ fV) t y hy
    refine ⟨W', h, hyW', c, hc.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ ↦ ?_)⟩
    rw [res_res]
    exact congrArg (fun a ↦ c k • a) (res_eq_res F _ _ _)
  have hκ : kernel.ι (freeToOver F (fun k ↦ res F fV (LP.gens k))) ≫ freeToOver G g = 0 := by
    refine hom_eq_zero_of_app_eq_zero _ fun Z w ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨⟨Wz, _rz, fz⟩⟩ := Z
    obtain ⟨e, he⟩ : ∃ e,
        (kernel.ι (freeToOver F (fun k ↦ res F fV (LP.gens k)))).val.app
          (op (Over.mk fz)) w = e := ⟨_, rfl⟩
    have h0 : (freeToOver F (fun k ↦ res F fV (LP.gens k))).val.app (op (Over.mk fz)) e = 0 := by
      rw [← he]
      exact (congrArg (fun m ↦ m.val.app (op (Over.mk fz)) w)
        (kernel.condition (freeToOver F (fun k ↦ res F fV (LP.gens k))))).trans
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.zero_app_apply _ w)
    have hz : ∑ k : LP.Gen, coords fz e k • res F (fz ≫ fV) (LP.gens k) = 0 := by
      rw [← ofCoords_coords fz e, freeToOver_app_ofCoords] at h0
      refine Eq.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ ↦ ?_) h0
      rw [res_res]
    change (freeToOver G g).val.app (op (Over.mk fz))
      ((kernel.ι (freeToOver F (fun k ↦ res F fV (LP.gens k)))).val.app
        (op (Over.mk fz)) w) = 0
    rw [he, ← ofCoords_coords fz e, freeToOver_app_ofCoords]
    refine eq_zero_of_locally_zero_mod G _ fun y hy ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨W', h, hyW', b, hb⟩ :=
      LP.relations (fz ≫ fV) (coords (R := structureSheaf Rc) fz e) hz y hy
    refine ⟨W', h, hyW', ?_⟩
    rw [res_sum_smul]
    refine sum_smul_eq_zero_of_relations _ b
      (fun l k ↦ resR (structureSheaf Rc) (h ≫ fz ≫ fV) (LP.rel l k)) _ (fun k ↦ ?_) (fun l ↦ ?_)
    · refine (hb k).trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun l _ ↦ ?_)
      exact congrArg (fun c ↦ b l * c) (resR_eq_resRLE _ _ _)
    · have h1 : res G h (res G fz (∑ k : LP.Gen,
          resR (structureSheaf Rc) fV (LP.rel l k) • g k)) = 0 := by
        rw [hrel l, res_zero, res_zero]
      rw [res_sum_smul, res_sum_smul] at h1
      refine Eq.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ ↦ ?_) h1
      refine congrArg (fun a ↦ a • res G h (res G fz (g k))) ?_
      rw [resR_resR, resR_resR]
      exact resR_eq_resRLE _ _ _
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ := exists_factor_of_epi _ (freeToOver G g) hκ
  refine ⟨φ, fun k ↦ ?_⟩
  have hu : ∀ (M : SheafOfModules.{v} (structureSheaf Rc)) (u : LP.Gen → M.val.obj (op V)),
      (freeToOver M u).val.app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 V)))
          (ofCoords (𝟙 V) (Pi.single k (1 : ToType ((structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj (op V)))))
        = u k := by
    intro M u
    rw [freeToOver_app_ofCoords, Finset.sum_eq_single_of_mem k (Finset.mem_univ k)
      (fun j _ hj ↦ by rw [Pi.single_eq_of_ne hj, zero_smul]), Pi.single_eq_same, one_smul,
      res_id]
  have e3 := congrArg (fun m ↦ m.val.app (op (Over.mk (𝟙 V)))
    (ofCoords (𝟙 V) (Pi.single k (1 : ToType ((structureSheaf Rc).obj.obj (op V)))))) hφ
  rw [hu G g] at e3
  exact (congrArg (φ.val.app _) (hu F fun k ↦ res F fV (LP.gens k)).symm).trans e3

/-- **Surjectivity half of Stacks 01CP, from a local presentation at `x`.** Every
`O_{X,x}`-homomorphism of stalks `F_x →ₗ G_x` is induced by a local homomorphism as soon as `F`
admits, on *some* neighbourhood of `x`, finitely many generating sections together with finitely
many relations generating all relations — which is exactly a
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalPresentation F x`. Nothing is assumed about `F` away from that
neighbourhood.

`surjective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap` is the global-hypothesis form, obtained by producing the local
presentation from `F` being of finite presentation. -/
theorem surjective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localPresentation (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X)
    (LP : LocalPresentation F x) : Function.Surjective (sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x) := by
  classical
  intro ψ
  obtain ⟨V, fV, hxV, g, hgerm, hrel⟩ := exists_gens_images LP ψ
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ := exists_hom_of_rel_zero LP fV g hrel
  refine ⟨germAt H.obj V x hxV ((H.sectionsEquiv V).symm φ), ?_⟩
  change sheafHomStalkMap H x (germAt H.obj V x hxV ((H.sectionsEquiv V).symm φ)) = ψ
  rw [sheafHomStalkMap_germ H V hxV, AddEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  refine linearMap_ext_gens LP fun k ↦ ?_
  rw [← hgerm k, stalkLinearMap_apply, ← germAt_resLE F fV.le hxV (LP.gens k),
    stalkMap_germ φ hxV le_rfl hxV]
  refine congrArg (germAt G V x hxV) ?_
  rw [← appAtR_eq_appAt, ← res_eq_resLE]
  exact hφ k

/-- **Surjectivity half of Stacks 01CP.** For `F` of finite presentation, every
`O_{X,x}`-homomorphism of stalks `F_x →ₗ G_x` is induced by a local homomorphism, i.e. is in the
image of the canonical map.

This is `surjective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localPresentation`, whose hypothesis is only that
`F` has a local presentation at `x`, applied to the presentation that finite presentation
produces there. -/
theorem surjective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X)
    [F.IsFinitePresentation] : Function.Surjective (sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x) :=
  (nonempty_localPresentation F x).elim
    (surjective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localPresentation H x)

/-- **Stacks 01CP at a single point.** The canonical map of Stacks 01CP is bijective as soon as
`F` admits a local presentation at `x`; no finiteness of `F` on the rest of the space is used.
Injectivity needs only the generators, surjectivity also the relations. -/
theorem bijective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localPresentation (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X)
    (LP : LocalPresentation F x) : Function.Bijective (sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x) :=
  ⟨injective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localGenerators H x LP.toLocalGenerators,
    surjective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap_of_localPresentation H x LP⟩

end LocalPresentationStalk

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01CP.** If `F` is of finite presentation, the canonical map from the
stalk of `SheafHom(F, G)` at `x` to the module of `O_{X,x}`-linear maps from `F_x` to `G_x` is an
isomorphism. The equivalence produced here is the canonical map `sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x`: its
`germ_apply` field records that it sends the germ of a local homomorphism and the germ of a local
section to the germ of the evaluation, and by `sheafHomStalkLinearMap_unique` that property
determines it. -/
@[stacks 01CP "finite_presentation_isomorphism"]
noncomputable def sheafHomStalkLinearEquivOfFinitePresentation
    (H : SheafHom Rc F G) (x : X) [F.IsFinitePresentation] :
    SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv Rc F G H x :=
  SheafHomStalkLinearEquiv.ofBijective H x
    ⟨injective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x, surjective_sheafHomStalkLinearMap H x⟩

end FinitePresentation

end Stacks.SheafOfModules.SheafHomStalk

